GROWTH GAPS

1. High-Stakes Narrative and Challenge Hooks
Top outlier creator @dhavalkataria_ (19.81% engagement) dominates by packaging technical business concepts into episodic, high-stakes financial challenges (e.g., "Can I make 50,000 using Raj Shamani's business idea?" or "Un-Broke-ing India"). In contrast, @garvit.irl focuses strictly on developer utility (free tokens, markdown skills), missing the broader aspirational audience motivated by income generation and career transformation.

2. Viral Visual Demonstrations over Abstract Architecture
Creators like @nick_saraev, @arshman, and @favourite.engineer achieve viral reach by demonstrating tangible visual outputs (e.g., Higgsfield Katana aura edits, reverse engineering full applications, generating 500+ motion design prompts). @garvit.irl primarily explains backend agent infrastructure and token repositories verbally, which lacks the instant visual gratification that drives shares and saves.

3. Breaking Trending GitHub Repositories at Speed
Competitors like @vaibhavsisinty and @nick_saraev instantly capitalize on breaking open-source trends (e.g., "Reverse Engineer Anything" crossing 40,000 GitHub stars). While @garvit.irl targets developer tools, covering repos before they peak gives competitors authority and broad algorithmic distribution.


RECOMMENDED ACTIONS

1. Pivot Format Exclusively to Video Reels Between 6:00 PM and 9:00 PM IST
Data shows Reels generate an average of 199 likes compared to static posts at only 30 likes (a 563% increase in engagement). Cease all static image posting for the next 7 days. Schedule all 3 to 4 planned Reels strictly within the proven peak window of 6:00 PM to 9:00 PM IST to maximize initial algorithm velocity.

2. Frame Technical Tutorials Around Concrete Monetary and Time Outcomes
Instead of positioning tools purely as technical skill files (e.g., "Ye simply ek markdown file hoti hai"), reframe the hook around direct replacement of expensive tools or costs (e.g., "How this free Claude tool replaces a 50,000 Rupee developer workflow"). Test this angle on trending tools like Claude Code plugins or Reverse Engineer Anything.

3. Standardize Automated Comment-to-DM Lead Magnets
Leverage the high comment baseline (median 127 comments) by embedding a single high-conversion trigger keyword in every video (e.g., "Comment AGENT to get the 5 GitHub repo links and prompts"). Deliver the bundle via DM to sustain comment ranking signals while capturing warm audience leads.
